    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75527" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁσι-ότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>disposition to observe divine law, piety,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				329c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				14d
			</span></i> sq., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.1.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				654
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				10
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς θεῶν ὁ.</span>
			<i>piety towards</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				34
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.359f
				</span></i>
			; also, like Lat. <i>pietas,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πρὸς γονεῖς ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					7.4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν τεκοῦσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					31.27
				</span></i>
			.</div>
